* dcs-buck-generic.lib - generic constant-on-time buck model
*
* An open behavioural model of a DCS-Control-class buck converter (constant
* on-time, ripple emulation from the switch node, a slow integrator for DC
* accuracy, valley comparator, minimum off-time, high-side peak and low-side
* valley current limits, optional power save). It is NOT a vendor model: the
* internals of TI's DCS-Control are not published. Its three free constants
* (KR, TR, GINT) and the on-time extension (ETH) were set so that, with
* TPS62136 parameters, it reproduces TI's own TPS62136 transient model
* (SLVMC09) in load step, ripple and loop gain; see README.md.
* Power-stage values come from the datasheets.
*
* Params:
*   TONSEL  1 = TON = VOUT/(VIN*FSW) (TPS62903 Eq. 3, 1 MHz)
*           2 = TON = KTON * VIN/(VIN-VOUT) (TPS62136 Eq. 1: KTON = 250 ns;
*               TPS62903 Eq. 5 with AEE at 2.5 MHz: KTON = 100 ns)
*   PFM     0 = forced PWM; 1 = power save (low side off at zero current)
*   ETH     on-time extension: the on-time continues while the FB-referred error
*           exceeds ETH [V] (large-signal behaviour; ETH=1 disables it)
*   FSW     nominal switching frequency [Hz] (TONSEL=1)
*   RHS RLS high- and low-side on-resistance [ohm]
*   ILIMH   high-side peak current limit [A]; ILIML low-side valley limit [A]
*   VREF    feedback reference [V]
*   TOFFMIN minimum off time [s]
*   KR      ripple-emulation gain [V/V]; TR ripple-emulation time constant [s]
*   GINT    integrator gain [1/s]
.subckt DCSBUCK vin sw vos fb gnd params: TONSEL=1 FSW=1e6 RHS=0.062 RLS=0.022
+ ILIMH=4.6 ILIML=4.4 VREF=0.6 TOFFMIN=80n KR=0.02 TR=2u GINT=2e4 KTON=250n PFM=0 ETH=5m
* ripple emulation: low-pass of (VSW - VOS)
Bx x gnd V = V(sw,gnd) - V(vos,gnd)
Rr x r 1k
Cr r gnd {TR/1k}
* integrator: DC accuracy loop
Bint gnd vint I = {GINT}*1n*(({VREF})-V(fb,gnd))
Cint vint gnd 1n
Rint vint gnd 1G
* integrator clamp: +/-20 mV at the reference (anti-windup)
Bclp vint gnd I = V(vint,gnd) > 0.02 ? (V(vint,gnd)-0.02)*0.1 : (V(vint,gnd) < -0.02 ? (V(vint,gnd)+0.02)*0.1 : 0)
* comparator (valley-type): turn on when FB + ramp falls below VREF + VINT
Bcmp cmp gnd V = ( ({VREF}) + V(vint,gnd) - V(fb,gnd) - {KR}*V(r,gnd) ) > 0 ? 1 : 0
* on-time ramp (V = microseconds since turn-on)
Bton gnd t I = V(q,gnd) > 0.5 ? 1m : -V(t,gnd)/10
Ct t gnd 1n
* off-time ramp
Btof gnd o I = V(q,gnd) > 0.5 ? -V(o,gnd)/10 : 1m
Co o gnd 1n
Btgt tgt gnd V = {TONSEL} < 1.5 ? 1e6*max(V(vos,gnd),0.1)/(max(V(vin,gnd),0.5)*{FSW}) : {KTON}*1e6*V(vin,gnd)/max(V(vin,gnd)-V(vos,gnd),0.05)
Bset set gnd V = (V(cmp,gnd) > 0.5 && V(o,gnd) > {TOFFMIN}*1e6 && I(Vil) < {ILIML}) ? 1 : 0
Bext ext gnd V = ( ({VREF}) + V(vint,gnd) - V(fb,gnd) - {KR}*V(r,gnd) ) > {ETH} ? 1 : 0
Brst rst gnd V = ((V(t,gnd) > V(tgt,gnd) && V(ext,gnd) < 0.5) || I(Vil) > {ILIMH}) ? 1 : 0
Bq qn gnd V = (V(rst,gnd) < 0.5 && (V(set,gnd) > 0.5 || V(q,gnd) > 0.5)) ? 1 : 0
Rq qn q 100
Cq q gnd 10p
* half bridge with on-resistance; inductor current is sensed by Vil (in series at SW)
* zero-current latch for power save: set when the low side reaches 0 A, cleared at turn-on
Bzn zn gnd V = ({PFM} > 0.5 && V(q,gnd) < 0.5 && (I(Vil) < 0 || V(z,gnd) > 0.5)) ? 1 : 0
Rz zn z 100
Cz z gnd 10p
Bsw swi gnd V = V(q,gnd) > 0.5 ? V(vin,gnd) - I(Vil)*{RHS} : (V(z,gnd) > 0.5 ? V(vos,gnd) : -I(Vil)*{RLS})
Vil swi sw 0
.ends DCSBUCK
